# Sigvault Desktop — build-time configuration
#
# `.env` at the repo root is NOT needed to run the app. OAuth client IDs and
# token URLs are per-environment and live in `BUILTIN_OAUTH_CLIENTS` in
# `crates/sigvault-core/src/env_config/mod.rs`, resolved at runtime from
# whichever environment the user selects. `cargo run -p sigvault-app` works
# from a clean clone.
#
# The only variables that matter at build time are the updater signing key and
# its password, and only when producing signed release artifacts. They keep
# their TAURI_* names because it is the same minisign key the earlier
# Tauri-based releases were signed with: installed copies of those verify
# updates against it. CI gets them from the `ENV_VARS_DESKTOP` GitHub secret,
# which the private `sigvault-secrets` repo owns
# (projects/desktop/development.env) and pushes here; `.ee.desktop` in this
# repo is the schema only, never the values.
#
# To sign installers locally, hand the key to cargo-packager:
#
#   export CARGO_PACKAGER_SIGN_PRIVATE_KEY="$TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY"
#   export CARGO_PACKAGER_SIGN_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD="$TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD"
#   cargo packager -p sigvault-app --release
#
# With the `ee` CLI and access to the secrets repo:
#
#   cd /path/to/sigvault-secrets/projects/desktop
#   eval "$(ee apply development --dry-run --format dotenv | sed 's/^/export /')"
#
# Note: API_BASE_URL and BITCOIN_NETWORK are not compile-time vars either. The
# app fetches the available environments at runtime from
# https://sigvault.org/environments.json and lets the user pick one before
# logging in.

TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=
